From 03d2cada26fb99cdf905c4ac96a1f207c3ba7667 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jd1100 <248791769+ayooooo123@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 13:43:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] test(private): do not require optional learned-closer
 grants

A real eleven-host run completed setup, activation, and the first routed immutable get, then waited forever for lookup-exit-a to emit isolated-grant-request. The event is optional: real DHT ordering returned the value without discovering a learned closer, while the local deterministic topology always takes the referral path.

Expose the total grant-request count in sanitized role snapshots. Keep standing responders for requests that arrive, but assert bounded accounting after each get rather than awaiting a mandatory event. This preserves 127 assertions in process:node and process:bare while allowing both valid DHT outcomes.
