Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(private): separate route lifetime from operation
 deadline

KI-4 Signature B came from a two-bound model representing three facts. An extension operation timeout shortened both its local deadline and the authenticated route wire expiry, invalidating limits the peer had already committed exactly at that expiry.

Carry an immutable authenticated wire expiry, its one-time coherent local projection, and a separately mutable operation deadline. Authenticated earlier wall expiries always project from the retained route pair. TailControl carries the final M3 monotonic high-water, rejects rollback, reserves one-shot transitions before injected clocks, enforces operation expiry again after the clock-bearing final route take, and destroys any captured transport across reentrant teardown.

No protocol frame, transcript, admitted-material key, or final-handoff key changes. Fresh reviewer/security review found no remaining findings after three correction rounds. Focused 78/78 tests and 573/573 assertions; full Node/Bare aggregates and all six Linux gates green.
