From 9d5a2b88f0329790870b48481a8fb44e05b6c641 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jd1100 <248791769+ayooooo123@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 15:23:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(test): reject mixed placements that require NAT
 hairpinning

Real mixed dispatches proved this workstation's NAT does not deliver packets between two local sockets through their shared reflected public address. Path diversity alone therefore permits placements whose required ALLOW_EDGES become silent. Mirror the exact allowed edge set in live-route.sh and reject any placement with both endpoints local before spending runner jobs.
---
 scripts/live-route.sh | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/live-route.sh b/scripts/live-route.sh
index b7de6eb03312f9734d7147180b740d3a71c604ca..3623341a3d1bd00bb00d5d14261d649630d7af4f 100755
--- a/scripts/live-route.sh
